From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 07:04:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: admin-forced facial recognition sharing between users

Admin action to directly merge a user into another account's cluster
group, bypassing the normal invite/accept flow that already exists
upstream (v3.2.0). Once merged, both accounts share the same named
(recognized) people across their libraries.

Concrete use case: P1 owns photos and has named people in them. Admin
wants P2 to see/benefit from that facial recognition without needing
P1 to send an invite and P2 to accept it.

- admin API: GET/PUT/DELETE /admin/users/:id/cluster-group/members,
  reusing personRepository.reassignCluster + userRepository.update -
  the exact same primitives the existing self-service accept/leave
  flow already uses and has tested
- web UI: new 'Facial Recognition Sharing' card on /admin/users/:id
- OpenAPI spec + @immich/sdk regenerated

Triggering the actual face detection/recognition ML jobs (if a
library hasn't been processed yet) does NOT need a fork patch - it's
already exposed to admins via the stock 'Jobs' admin page (Face
Detection / Facial Recognition, with a 'force' re-run option).

Based on immich-app/immich@b26b0cc

Fork-Patch: 0002-admin-cluster-group-merge
